From c99bc48c3b217d89c4613b9b0dd34fcf737ab341 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 18 Sep 2026 19:37:30 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] Content: tire rotation guide for all six catalog vehicles
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Adds the first premium guide to the five vehicles that had nothing to
sell — Civic, F-150, Silverado, Sierra and Escape were free-guide-only,
so a per-vehicle unlock would have bought the user nothing.

Written as one universal template applied per vehicle, per the platform
-template approach in the content scaling strategy. The only per-vehicle
inputs are drivetrain (which picks the cross pattern), lug nut torque,
base tire size, jack points and the TPMS reset procedure.

All torque values are the curated lug nut specs already carried in each
vehicle's specs list — no new numbers were invented, and no Open Labor
Project quota was spent. The guides correctly fail the admin console's
"provenance" recommended check, which puts all six on the Build Queue
for a sourced-data pass later. That is intended, not an oversight.

Tier: premium on all six. The oil change stays the single free hook per
vehicle, so the free-guide invariant is unchanged (verified: all six
vehicles still have exactly one free guide). This same template becomes
the free hook on EVs per claude/ev-free-guide-decision-2026-09-18.md.

Three new original schematic illustrations in the existing house style:
forward-cross and rearward-cross rotation patterns, and a tread depth
check. Rasterized and visually verified — the first draft had the cross
arrows terminating in empty space and was redrawn.

Verified: next build compiles clean; all 13 guides pass every required
validation check in src/lib/admin/guides.ts; 13 unique guide ids; all 18
referenced step illustrations exist on disk; eslint unchanged at the same
4 pre-existing problems (confirmed identical with the change stashed).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
